  "comment": "**What it does**\nFinds **good businesses that are temporarily cheap** - value WITH proof of\nlife, so cheap-for-a-reason value traps get skipped.\n- **Cheap** - 20%+ below the intrinsic-value models AND a lower P/E than its\n  own industry, PEG 1.5 or less (trailing or forward).\n  (The brief said ~30% safety margin - that plus every quality gate left only\n  8 names; 20% hits the target list size. Raise it back for stricter value.)\n- **Good** - ROIC 8%+ (brief said ~10 - softened a notch for list size) and\n  passing the yearly health checklist. Profitable only.\n- **Proof of life** - at (or within 5% of) the 200-day line: the market has\n  stopped voting no.\n$1B and bigger.\n\n**How to tweak**\n- More names? Drop the P/E-vs-industry block.\n- Stricter value? `margin_of_safety` to 30-40 and `roic` to 12.\n\n**How to sort for best picks**\n- **Sort by `value_score`**, tiebreak `quality_score` (quality confirms the\n  bargain is real).\n- **Avoid** `momentum_score` - freshly-recovering value names rarely lead on\n  price action yet; sorting by it re-buries the bargains.",
  "ai_instructions": "Find good businesses that are temporarily cheap \u2014 value WITH proof of life, so I\nskip the value traps (cheap companies that deserve to be cheap).\n- **Goal**: value. **Dividends**: ignore.\n- **Cheap**: trading well below fair value (margin of safety ~30%+) AND cheaper\n  than its own industry.\n- **Good**: real profitability (ROIC ~10%+) and passing basic health checks \u2014\n  profitable companies only.\n- **Proof of life**: price at least back above its 200-day average, so the market\n  has stopped voting against it.\n- **Size**: $1B and bigger. **Kinds**: normal stocks only. **Risk**: moderate.\n- **Results**: ~20-150 names. **Sorting**: value first, tiebreak quality.",
